# =============================================================================
# DeskMedia Display - git ignore policy
#
#   NOTHING secret, personal, large or device-specific is ever pushed:
#     * factory flash dumps stay on the maintainer's own machines (see docs/development-history/M0-factory-backup.md)
#     * Wi-Fi passwords, the pairing key and any tokens live only in the device's NVS, in the companion's
#       per-user (DPAPI-protected) data folder or in local, ignored files - never in source, logs or commits
#     * vendor downloads and build output are re-creatable (see docs/development.md)
#
#   If a rule here blocks something that really must be committed (e.g. a firmware
#   asset that happens to be a .bin), add a narrow "!negation" below or `git add -f`
#   it - and say why in the commit message.
# =============================================================================

# --- 1. FACTORY FIRMWARE / FLASH DUMPS (never push) --------------------------------
# The whole-chip backup is a 16 MiB, device-specific image: it is never committed, only the
# procedure for making and restoring one (docs/development-history/M0-factory-backup.md, backup/README.md) is.
backup/*
!backup/README.md
backup/**/*.bin
*.bin
*.dump
*.img
*.rom
*.nvs

# --- 2. SECRETS, CREDENTIALS, PERSONAL CONFIG (never push) -------------------------
# Wi-Fi passwords, the pairing key, access/refresh tokens, authorization codes, client secrets,
# private keys. Only templates named *.example.* may be committed.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets.*
!secrets.example.*
secrets.local.h
*.secret
*.secrets
*.local
*.local.*
!*.local.example
!*.local.example.*
sdkconfig.local
sdkconfig.local.*
local.properties
credentials*.json
credentials*.txt
client_secret*.json
wifi*.json
wifi*.txt
*token*.json
*token*.txt
*token*.dat
*token*.env
*.token
*.tokens
pairing*.dat
pairing*.json
**/pairing/
*.dpapi
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# --- 3. ESP-IDF BUILD OUTPUT (re-creatable) ----------------------------------------
# firmware/dependencies.lock is NOT ignored on purpose: it pins the exact component versions.
build/
managed_components/
sdkconfig
sdkconfig.old
compile_commands.json

# --- 4. LOCAL TOOLCHAINS / VIRTUALENVS / CACHES (re-creatable) ---------------------
tools/venv/
venv/
.venv/
.espressif/
.cache/
.ccache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# --- 5. LARGE VENDOR DOWNLOADS (re-fetch per README; third-party licensed) ---------
docs/waveshare/

# --- 6. LOGS / CAPTURES / TEMPORARY FILES ------------------------------------------
# Serial logs can contain Wi-Fi names, device IDs or (if a bug logs them) tokens.
*.log
logs/
captures/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.swp
*~
eim.log

# --- 7. EDITOR / OS / AGENT-LOCAL FILES --------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.local.*

# Companion packaging output (PyInstaller)
dist/
*.spec

# --- 9. PERSONAL IDLE-SCREEN CUSTOMISATION (never push) --------------------------------------------------------------
# The companion keeps a user's idle screen (settings file + chosen picture) in %LOCALAPPDATA%\DeskMediaCompanion\idle, outside the
# repository. These patterns catch the same files (and any personal photo / theme asset) should they ever end up inside a checkout,
# e.g. through `--data-dir`. A personalised theme is a local asset, not part of the generic product.
**/idle/settings.json
**/idle/background.jpg
**/idle/original.bin
**/idle-assets/
**/personal/
**/private/
*.private.*
idle-settings*.json
idle_background*
